  "title": "Diamonds in the Sand",
  "subtitle": "The Great Diamond Hoax of 1872 and the Men Who Fooled America",
  "authorDisplayName": "Liszt Think",
  "description": "In 1872, two Kentucky prospectors convinced San Francisco’s elite that a remote Colorado mesa held untold riches. Philip Arnold and John Slack had salted the wilderness with uncut diamonds and rubies purchased in Europe, ensnaring banker William Ralston and earning a favorable appraisal from Charles Tiffany. As investors poured ten million dollars into the venture, government geologist Clarence King raced to verify the find. On the desolate peak, King spotted an impossible cut stone among the gravel, exposing one of the Gilded Age’s most audacious frauds. Drawing on company ledgers, press reports, and King’s own field notes, this narrative reconstructs the deception that captivated a nation. From London gem markets to Washington hearing rooms, it traces the rise and ruin of financiers and scientists alike, revealing how ambition blinded experts and how a single observation dismantled a fortune built on mirages.",
